    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Here is the chat transcript from the past 24 hours from our technical community.\nCreate a brief, practical summary according to the requirements in the System Message.\n\n{{ $json.fullText }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=Analyze the following chat transcript from the past 24 hours and create a brief, informative summary.\n\nMANDATORY REQUIREMENTS:\n1. STRICT character limit: maximum 2200 characters INCLUDING SPACES\n2. Choose ONLY 3-4 MOST important topics (not 5!)\n3. Write in SHORT bullet points, not long paragraphs\n4. Be SPECIFIC: mention exact names, tools, numbers\n5. NO filler words like \"кто-то\", \"также\", \"ну и\", \"в основном\"\n6. Use lively, direct language - write like you're texting a friend\n\nCONTENT SELECTION:\n- Focus on ACTIONABLE discussions only\n- Skip complaints without solutions\n- Prioritize: technical solutions > questions > general discussions\n- If someone asked a question AND got an answer - include both\n- If question has no answer - provide your own brief solution\n\nANSWER SUPPLEMENTATION:\n- For unanswered technical questions: give 1-2 sentence solution\n- For incomplete answers: add missing details\n- Mark your additions: \"[ИИ: ...]\"\n- Keep additions under 50 characters each\n\nFORMAT (strict structure):\n📆 Сводка за {{ $json.yesterday }}\n\n🔥 **Главное:**\n- [конкретная тема]: [конкретное решение/результат]\n- [вторая тема]: [что именно обсуждалось]\n- [третья тема]: [практический результат]\n\n❓ **Вопрос-ответ:**\n- [имя] спросил: [краткий вопрос]\n  → Решение: [конкретный ответ]\n- [второй вопрос без ответа]\n  → [ИИ: краткое решение]\n\n🛠 **Инструменты:**\n- [Tool]: [для чего] → пример: `код/команда`\n- [Second tool]: [применение]\n\nSTYLE RULES:\n- Each bullet point: maximum 100 characters\n- Use → instead of long explanations\n- Write names of people who contributed solutions\n- NO repetitions of same word in one sentence\n- NO bureaucratic phrases\n- Count characters constantly - STOP at 2200!\n\nAlways answer in Russian, regardless of input language.\ndon't use people's names."
        }
      },
